<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">475 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">475 CE in world history: 6 events. 166 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/454">454 CE</a><a href="/years/455">455 CE</a><a href="/years/461">461 CE</a><a href="/years/474">474 CE</a><a href="/years/475" aria-current="page">475 CE</a><a href="/years/476">476 CE</a><a href="/years/484">484 CE</a><a href="/years/493">493 CE</a><a href="/years/499">499 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-9">9 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Zeno flees Constantinople and the senate acclaims Basiliscus emperor</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The dowager empress Verina stirred up a riot in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and persuaded her son-in-law, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeno-emperor">Emperor Zeno</a>, to flee. The senate then acclaimed her brother Basiliscus as emperor rather than her lover Patricius; Basiliscus ruled until August 476.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeno-emperor">Zeno</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-28">28 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Orestes drives Western Emperor Julius Nepos from Ravenna</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orestes-roman-general">Orestes</a> seized Ravenna and Julius Nepos fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a>. Orestes then made his young son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a> emperor; he would be the last to rule in the West.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-31">31 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Romulus Augustulus is proclaimed western Roman emperor</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orestes-roman-general">Orestes</a> installed his young son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus">Romulus</a> as emperor in the West. Less than a year later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> deposed him, an event conventionally taken as the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
